course: dictionary
lesson: 1505
title: Words for special days
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To celebrate means to do something special and enjoyable because of a happy event, such as a birthday, a festival or a win. «Diwali is the festival of lights, celebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains with lamps, sweets and fireworks.» The clues are lamps, sweets and fireworks, so celebrated means marked with a happy, festive time.
explain: Celebrate can also mean to praise or honour someone in public. «At school, we celebrate achievements in assemblies» means the school shows and cheers what pupils have done well. Check by swapping in your meaning: "we praise achievements in assemblies" still makes sense.
explain: Celebrated can also be an adjective meaning famous. «Kyiv celebrated 1,500 years in 1982» uses the word for a party-like event, and the date was a chosen round number, because nobody knows the exact founding year.
fact: To celebrate means to do something special and enjoyable for a happy event or a special day.
fact: «Celebrate» can also mean to praise or honour someone or something publicly.
fact: «Celebrated» can be an adjective meaning famous.
fact: Useful phrases are «celebrate a birthday», «celebrate success» and «something to celebrate».
fact: Respecting how others celebrate, such as Eid, Hanukkah or Matariki, is part of being kind.
exercise: «Diwali is the festival of lights, celebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains.» What does celebrated mean here? | *Marked with a special, happy festival | Cancelled because of rain | Hidden away from everyone | Made out of light
exercise: «At school, we celebrate achievements in assemblies.» What does celebrate mean here? | To buy new books | To forget about | *To praise and honour in public | To be quiet about
exercise: «She is a celebrated author, read by children all over the world.» What does celebrated mean? | Very tired | *Famous | Poor | Lost
test: Which is a good way to celebrate a birthday? | Hide the cake and say nothing | Turn off the lights and sleep | *Have a party with friends and family | Cry because you are older
test: «Respecting how others celebrate is part of being kind.» What does this suggest? | Everyone must celebrate in the same way | Birthdays are not important | Other people's festivals should be ignored | *Showing care for other people's special days
exam: «Our team won the cup, so let's ___!» Which word fits best? | Hide | Sleep | Forget it | *Celebrate
